WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.083
- So at Khan Academy,

00:00:04.083 --> 00:00:07.150
we are striving to create personalized

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.750
mastery based learning that
transforms student's mindsets.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.820
And within that I think
there's a three things

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.120
that make our value proposition unique.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.930
The first is that our content
is provided free of charge

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.790
for teachers and students.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.400
The second is that we have custom content

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.780
that's aligned to standards
in different countries.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.350
So in Brazil, to the BNCC.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.760
Or in the US, to the common core.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.388
And the third is that

00:00:31.388 --> 00:00:34.260
we are a technology that's not just

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.180
a substitute for paper and pencil,

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.300
and not such a dramatic change

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.740
that it'd be overwhelming

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.200
and you'd have to rethink
everything in your classroom,

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.440
but right in the middle

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.630
to offer an innovative change

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.743
that is not too overwhelming for teachers.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.140
For us at Khan Academy,

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.430
mastery learning is fairly simple.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.610
It's that the incentives,
the decisions in class

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.280
should be made based on what students

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:04.640
are proving they understand consistently.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.290
And in many cases that happens in tests,

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.950
maybe not 'til the end of year tests,

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.180
but we think it should
be a full year process

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.040
building up to that point.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.680
Really it's not like a yes or no,

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.230
are you fully mastery based

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:18.910
or are you not at all mastery based,

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:21.190
there's a spectrum of ways you can

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:24.140
change over your classroom
to be more mastery based.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.380
When it comes to personalization though,

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.500
there's a few things that
are really important.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.090
The first is that there's the
right content for students.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.210
And that might not be the same

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:34.900
for all students in the class.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.860
And we can help personalize that content,

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.000
but at the end of the
day it is the teacher

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.780
that's going to be most effective

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:45.070
at personalizing the
content using Khan Academy.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.400
And second, it's self-paced.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.740
So that if I need more
practice on a given topic,

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:51.573
I can have it.

00:01:51.573 --> 00:01:53.260
I can have what we sometimes call

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.660
a functionally infinite
amount of practice.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:56.493
If you're not getting it,

00:01:56.493 --> 00:01:58.240
try again, no problem.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.170
Well when we think about
the student mindset

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.050
that we'd all hope to have,

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.180
both for ourselves and for our students,

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:07.800
I think it's a student
that believes strongly

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:08.778
in their own potential,

00:02:08.778 --> 00:02:10.958
and has the learning strategies

00:02:10.958 --> 00:02:14.240
to actually understand difficult material.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.770
And so there's a few ways we
try to enable that mindset

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.380
for learners on our platform.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.490
The first is to remove
all barriers to learning.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.670
So there's the content accessible

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:26.870
for all students at all times,

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.977
and then there's support
while you're practicing

00:02:28.977 --> 00:02:30.470
if you get stuck.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:34.010
And so there's no excuse
to not start learning,

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.430
and to not persist when you're stuck.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.100
The focus is on you.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:42.610
The second though is
processes to get unstuck,

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:43.950
for lack of a better word.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.320
And so you're in the middle
of learning and you're stuck,

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:47.560
which is totally fine.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.620
It's normal, happens to everyone.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.410
But right below the practice

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:52.650
it's gonna say are you stuck?

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.483
Get help.

00:02:53.483 --> 00:02:55.290
There's multiple ways
that you might need help.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.480
You maybe need a hint, you
maybe need to watch a video,

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.580
you might need to ask your teacher.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.090
But by going through that process,

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.290
you figure out when the right time is

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.360
to use each of those strategies.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.680
And then the third is
through encouragement

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.130
that we give on the site,

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.630
whether you're getting
problems right or wrong,

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.296
that reinforces the message

00:03:13.296 --> 00:03:15.593
that it's the effort that counts.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.130
Student agency is a really popular

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.160
topic right now in education,

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:26.660
and I think that sometimes
there's a mistake

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:31.010
that it's going from no
agency to total agency.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.910
But we really see it as a spectrum.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:34.950
And on Khan Academy at a minimum,

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.971
the agency that we think is
important for students to have

00:03:37.971 --> 00:03:40.640
would be to answer some questions like

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.720
am I on track to complete
these assignments?

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.470
What order am I gonna work on them?

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:47.400
And when do I know if I need help?

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.550
But as you start to show more maturity,

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:53.010
being able to take
control a little bit more

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.440
of the learning process,

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.140
then you can start to make
some bigger decisions.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.280
Like what's my actual goal for this week,

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.210
or this month, or the whole school year?

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:03.520
What matters to me?

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.280
And when I'm done with this content,

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.280
are there other subjects
that I want to explore

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.340
on my own that aren't even required?

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:13.670
So the learning experience
on Khan Academy.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:16.410
Well it could be different
from student to student,

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:19.980
I like to think of one student's
experience in particular.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.430
So his name is Damien,

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:25.110
he's an 11 year old in southern
California, Los Angeles,

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.680
but I think his experience could

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.470
be typical of students in Sao Paolo,

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.210
or anywhere around the world.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.230
But there were a few
things about his experience

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.330
that I think were really important,

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.080
and that I took away from

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.570
the ideal experience on Khan Academy.

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.740
So the first is that he had a
really clear goal for the year

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.750
that his teacher had provided
for him on Khan Academy.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.550
And every time he logged in,

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.380
the first thing he saw was

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.690
his progress toward that big goal.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:54.474
But combined with that big goal,

00:04:54.474 --> 00:04:56.420
each day as he was practicing,

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.810
he had really detailed support,

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.920
both instructional support

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:02.760
through the videos and articles,

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.310
and then the practice support

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:08.210
through the exercises and
challenges and unit tests.

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:09.043
And not only that,

00:05:09.043 --> 00:05:11.180
but he also had his
teacher there as a resource

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:14.152
if the instructional
resources weren't enough.

00:05:14.152 --> 00:05:18.290
And there was this combination
of his teacher, Ms Choo

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:21.710
being an expert about
how to use Khan Academy,

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.740
but also Damien having
some freedom and choice

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:27.480
and agency to move on if he was done.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.760
To have his own freedom to choose

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.150
what he was gonna work on that day.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.770
So that balance between the teacher

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:36.290
really being able to guide
Damien towards the right material

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.470
but him also having freedom and control

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.540
over his learning process.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.550
So you've got the big goal
and the detailed support,

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:45.300
and you've got the teacher as the expert,

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.560
but the student still having the freedom.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:48.870
And that's I think what makes

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.873
the learning experience
distinct on Khan Academy.

